            <ArticleTitle>Anomalous origin of the right coronary artery from the left sinus of Valsalva: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>334-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The rare anomalous origin of the right coronary artery from the left sinus of Valsalva has recently been shown to be associated with myocardial ischemia and sudden death. A patient is presented with overwhelming evidence of myocardial ischemia corrected by a single-vessel bypass of the right coronary artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
